0..76 Comment "/// An indexed family `Skip` carries an operation `skip` and a rule over it."
77..80 Comment "///"
81..229 Comment "/// Each node of the operation and the rule answers at its own span. The editor reads an indexed family\'s members as it reads an unindexed family\'s."
230..233 Comment "///"
234..513 Comment "/// The checker admits `Skip`, and the operation routes no function, since a route\'s port is a family at no index. The described reading gives each port the family at the index the port writes. The family states no expectation, since the sugared form drops an own-line attribute."
